===persian===

کارگاهم...
پُرِ مهتابِ زمستانی است...
تب دارم... عشق در خاطرم گرم می‌بارد...
من نمی‌دانم اَبر،
من نمی‌دانم آب،
من نمی‌دانم مهتاب... چه رازی دارد...
هرچه عاشق‌تر باشی...
اَبر غمگین‌تر...
آب آبی‌تر...
مهتاب... مهتابی‌تر...
۱۳۷۰/۹/۲۷

===machine===

My studio...
is full of winter moonlight...
I have a fever... love rains warm in my memory...
I do not know what secret the cloud,
I do not know what secret the water,
I do not know what secret the moonlight holds...
The more in love you are...
the sadder the cloud...
the bluer the water...
the moonlight... the more moonlit...
1370/9/27

===lantern===

My studio...
is full of winter moonlight...
I have a fever... love comes down warm in my memory...
I do not know what the cloud,
I do not know what the water,
I do not know what the moonlight has for a secret...
The more in love you are —
the sadder the cloud,
the bluer the water,
the moonlight... the more moonlit...

1370/9/27

===translation===

===footnotes===

The last rung of the ladder is a tautology and means to be: cloud goes sadder,
water goes bluer, and moonlight simply goes *more moonlit* — مهتاب، مهتابی‌تر. Loving harder does
not transform the moonlight into something else; it makes it more entirely what it already was.

